hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1363","Muhammad bin Ali bin Mahrez and Ahmad bin Al-Azhar told us, they said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ja`far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the prayer of fear with the same Al-Riqa’, she said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut the people into two fists, and a group lined up behind him, and a group stood up and faced the enemy. She said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” and the group who were lined up behind him said “Allahu Akbar,” then he bowed and they bowed, then he prostrated and they prostrated, then he raised his head. So they rose, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained seated and prostrated themselves the second prostration, then they got up and turned on their heels. They walked backwards, until they stood up behind them, and the other group approached, Ahmad said: and they all said: So line up behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said the salutation, so they said “Allahu Akbar”, then they bowed for themselves, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated his second prostration, and they prostrated Al-Azhar: So they prostrated with him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up in his rak’ah, and they prostrated for themselves the second prostration, then the The two groups gathered together, and they said: So they lined up behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he bowed with them one rak’ah and they all bowed, then he prostrated and they all prostrated, he said Abu Al-Azhar: Then he raised his head and they raised with him, and Muhammad bin Ali said: They raised his place, and he did not say: Then he raised his head, and they all said: He was That came from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, very quickly. They did not hope that he would mitigate it as much as he could. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him. So they greeted them, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and the people joined him in all of his prayers.”"
